  <p>The vertical gain is 30 percent of the straight-line path length. This is an idealised geometric example, not a complete flight-navigation calculation.</p>

  <h3>Example 13: A Diagonal Mechanical Brace</h3>
  <p>A diagonal brace has a length of 2 m and a vertical component of 1.6 m. The brace is the hypotenuse, <span set:html={rich('[[c=2\\,\\text{m}]]')} />, and the vertical component is the opposite side, <span set:html={rich('[[a=1.6\\,\\text{m}]]')} />:</p>
  <p><span set:html={rich('[[\\sin(A)=\\frac{1.6}{2}]]')} /></p>
