  <p>The vertical difference is 60 percent of the line-of-sight distance. The result does not give the tree's total height above ground unless the observer's eye height and other necessary information are accounted for.</p>

  <p>Sine is a mathematical ratio, not a physical quantity with units. Its practical value comes from comparing a vertical or perpendicular component with a sloping distance, calculating components when the angle is known, and verifying geometric relationships. Do not treat sine alone as a certificate of structural safety, load capacity, accessibility, or engineering compliance.</p>

